style(workspace): zero out clippy `-D warnings` across all targets and features

Sweep every clippy lint surfaced by the workspace-strict
`pedantic` / `nursery` / `cargo` groups plus the project-specific
restrictions (`unwrap_used`, `expect_used`, `clone_on_ref_ptr`,
`option_if_let_else`, `shadow_unrelated`, `large_enum_variant`,
`allow_attributes_without_reason`, ...). Both
`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` and
`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
now exit clean.

Code-level fixes:
* `corx-core::config::SsrfMode::admits_private` takes `self` by value
  (it is `Copy`).
* `corx-core::error::ErrorKind::status` merges three arms that all
  map to `BAD_GATEWAY`.
* `corx-core::proxy::mod` and `cors::apply_to_error_response` doc
  comments split their long first paragraph.
* `corx-core::proxy::cors::request` test helper renames the
  parameters that shadowed the outer `method` binding.
* `corx-core::proxy::forwarded::inject` takes `ForwardedConfig` by
  value; the surrounding `append_xff` helper uses `map_or_else`
  instead of nested `match`. All test sites and `corx-server`
  handlers updated.
* `corx-core::proxy::redirect::NextHop::Continue` now boxes its
  `Request` payload to keep the enum discriminant pointer-sized;
  the single call site in `Upstream::execute` dereferences the box.
* `corx-core::proxy::upstream::Upstream::new` is now infallible
  (`-> Self`), the `rustls-platform-verifier` import lives at the
  module top, and `ServerBuild::from_config` no longer propagates a
  redundant `?`.
* `corx-core::proxy::url_parser` flips the URL-construction helpers
  to `Option::map_or_else` and drops a redundant equality guard.
* `corx-server::handlers::shape_response` returns `Response`
  directly (no needless `Result` wrap); `parts` / `body` bindings
  renamed to avoid shadowing; `append_via_header` uses
  `map_or_else`.
* `corx-server::observability::metering::poll_frame` flattens the
  nested success branch with a let-else.
* `corx-server::hot_reload::ServerBuild::hot_reload` uses
  `Arc::clone` explicitly; tests `drop()` the install-default
  `Result`; the non-Unix `watch_sighup` stub spells out its
  `unused_async` reason.
* `corx-server::middleware::origin_guard::tests::make` takes
  `&SecurityConfig`; `rate_limit::build_host` takes the `Copy`
  config by value.
* `corx-server::router::build_router` drops a redundant `must_use`.
* `corx::main` declares `print_stdout` allowed (CLI design) and
  swaps an `Arc.clone()` for `Arc::clone(&...)`.

Test/bench wiring:
* `crates/corx-core/benches/{url_parser,ssrf_guard}.rs` carry an
  explicit `#![allow(...)]` block with a `reason = "..."` covering
  `unused_crate_dependencies`, `missing_docs` (criterion macros),
  and the restriction lints that are inappropriate for benches.
* `crates/corx-server/tests/integration_proxy.rs` carries the same
  rationale plus `tests_outside_test_module` for cargo's
  integration-test convention.

Cargo manifest:
* `crates/corx-core` declares the two new bench targets with
  `harness = false` and pulls `criterion` into `dev-dependencies`;
  `corx-core::lib.rs` carries a `#[cfg(test)] use criterion as _;`
  anchor so the workspace `unused_crate_dependencies` lint stays
  green at the library level.

80 tests passing under `cargo test --workspace --all-features`.
